# WebAssembly Component Model

Normative specs (implement these; do not invent a parallel ABI):

- Binary: [Binary.md](https://github.com/WebAssembly/component-model/blob/main/design/mvp/Binary.md)
- Canonical ABI: [CanonicalABI.md](https://github.com/WebAssembly/component-model/blob/main/design/mvp/CanonicalABI.md)
- WIT: [WIT.md](https://github.com/WebAssembly/component-model/blob/main/design/mvp/WIT.md)

## Binary vs core

A `.wasm` file is either a **core module** (layer 0) or a **component** (layer 1). Lovelace’s default output is a **component**.

| | Magic | Version / layer (bytes 4–7) |
|---|---|---|
| Core module | `00 61 73 6D` (`\0asm`) | `01 00 00 00` (version 1, layer 0) |
| Component | `00 61 73 6D` | `0D 00 01 00` (version `0x0d`, layer 1) |

Component sections (do not reuse core section IDs at the component layer): custom `0`, core module `1`, core instance `2`, core type `3`, nested component `4`, instance `5`, alias `6`, type `7`, canon `8`, start `9`, import `10`, export `11`, value `12`.

Version `0x0d` is pre-standard; follow the spec if it bumps.

## WIT / WAT / WASM

- **WIT** — IDL (`package ns:name@version;`, `interface`, `world`). Companion file the compiler always generates.
- **WAT** — text form of the component: `(component ...)` with `(core module ...)`, `(canon lift ...)`, `(canon lower ...)`.
- **WASM** — binary the runtime loads.

WIT `string` / `list` / `record` / `variant` are **not** core types. Core only has `i32`/`i64`/`f32`/`f64` and linear memory.

## Canonical ABI (mandatory)

- **`canon lift`**: wrap a core func as a component export (host/component → core: allocate via `cabi_realloc`, write memory, pass ptr/len).
- **`canon lower`**: wrap a component import so core can call it (core → host: read ptr/len from guest memory).

Typical lowering (implement per Canonical ABI, not this sketch):

- `string` / `list<T>` → stack `(i32 ptr, i32 len)`; memory 8-byte fat pointer
- small `record` → flattened scalars if ≤ 16 flats; else pointer
- `variant` / `option` / `result` → discriminant + payload (alignment/padding per spec)
- `resource` → `i32` handle, not a raw pointer

Always emit the core `memory` and `cabi_realloc` the ABI requires for lifted results.

## Custom metadata

When a component needs host-native functions beyond WASI, the compiler may emit:

- WIT doc annotations such as `@native` / `@native(provider="lib….so")`
- a component **custom section** named `love:native_imports` listing native libraries/symbols

The JIT reads these **before** instantiate. Do not put native policy only in undocumented side files.

## Embedded documentation

Public Lovelace doc-comments must be representable in the emitted artifacts:

- **WIT** — interface/function documentation (`///` or equivalent attributes)
- **WAT** — matching annotations so text dumps stay documented
- **WASM** — custom section and/or component attributes (do not strip docs)

Keep native-import metadata and human docs in distinct custom sections/attributes.